pressure has been the key motivator. I used to be the only one in my family who wanted to play the flute. My mother used to say that even if I didn't become a doctor, I would end up being a fruit seller and that would be the worst of all. It was a kind of pressure, but it also pushed me forward. I used to say to myself, "If I can't become a doctor, I must become a doctor of music, a doctor of the soul."
How did you feel when you had to leave the country and live abroad? Do you feel nostalgic about being in India? You're a citizen of India, so do you feel that Indian culture is a big part of your identity?
Yes, I do. The music I play is influenced by the sounds of India. I believe the depth of Indian culture is something that even the West can't imitate. The soul of India lies in its music. It's more than just being a citizen;
